{"v":1,"id":"sikafloor-multiduret-14","n":"Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14","b":"Sika","u":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/flooring/resin-flooring/epoxy-flooring-productssystems/epoxy-flooring-systems/sikafloor-multiduret-14.html","c":"construction/flooring/resin-flooring/epoxy-flooring-productssystems/epoxy-flooring-systems","d":{"t":"High build 100% solids textured-non slip epoxy coating system","s":"Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14 is pigmented durable, high build, textured epoxy floor coating system. It also provides unique non blooming/whitening properties when exposed to moisture early in curing and/or in lower cure environments. Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14 can also be used vertically on coves and walls.","a":["Light to medium mechanical resistance","Medium chemical resistance","Increased slip resistance","Non blooming/whitening","Texture varied to suit application","Easy cleanability"],"us":["Automotive workshops","Education - Trade work areas.","Stadiums","Correctional facilities","Amenities and change-rooms","Manufacturing, Packing and processing, light to medium duty","Car parks - intermediate and lower decks"],"pk":"","sec":[{"l":"APPROVALS / CERTIFICATES","t":"Textures - Conforms to AS 4586-2013 P Ratings VOC - Australian Standards ASTM D3960 Gren Star Building Council V2 IEQ-13 V1 IEQ-11 Cleanability “Excellent” (VDMA “Riboflavin test for low germ or sterile process technologies” tested). Slip resistance class R9 in accordance with DIN 51130 and BGR 181. Conforms to the requirements of EN 13813 and EN 1504-2 Fire Classification Australia - Critical Radiant Flux - Pass AS/ISO 9239.1 AP VS0209 appendix B Fire classification in accordance with EN 13501-1, Report-No. KB-Hoch-170419, Hoch Fladungen, Germany, March 2017","g":"Sustainability / Certifications / Approvals"},{"l":"System structure","t":"Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14 1. Primer (Optional) | Sikafloor-161/-160 2. Wearing Coats | 1 x Sikafloor-264 1 x Sikafloor -264T AU Note: Addition of 60 or 80 mesh aluminium oxide incorporated into the final coat at 5-6%vol will produce additional texture The addition of primer is subject to total film thickeness and substrate conditions.","g":"System information"},{"l":"Composition","t":"Epoxy","g":"System information"},{"l":"Nominal thickness","t":"~ 0.5mm to 0.7mm","g":"System information"},{"l":"Shore D Hardness","t":"~76 (7 days / +23 °C) | (DIN 53 505)","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Compressive strength","t":"Resin : ~60 N/mm2 (28 days / +23 °C) | (EN 196–1)","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Tensile adhesion strength","t":"> 1.5 N/mm² (failure in concrete) | (ISO 4624)","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Reaction to fire","t":"Critical radiant flux - Pass | AS/ISO 9239.1 AP VS0209 Appendix B","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Chemical resistance","t":"Resistant to many chemicals. Please ask for a detailed chemical resistance table.","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Skid / slip resistance","t":"P1 to P4 (depending on texture approach) | AS 4586 -2013","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Material temperature","t":"Please refer to the individual Product Data Sheet","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Ambient air temperature","t":"+10 °C min. / +30 °C max.","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Relative air humidity","t":"80 % r.h. max.","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Substrate temperature","t":"+10 °C min. / +30 °C max.","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Substrate moisture content","t":"When performing application work with Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14, the substrate moisture content must not exceed 4 % pbw measured by Tramex. Test method: Sika-Tramex meter, CM - measurement or Oven-dry-method. No rising moisture according to ASTM (Polyethylene-sheet). Use Sikafloor 161 Primer for moisture to 6%pbw. For >6%pbw use EpoCem 81.","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Waiting time to overcoating","t":"Before applying Sikafloor–264 anfd 264T AU on Sikafloor 161/–160 allow: Substrate temperature | Minimum | Maximum +10 °C | 24 hours | 3 days +20 °C | 12 hours | 2 days +30 °C | 8 hours | 1 day Note: For faster intercoat times use Sikafloor Booster - Refer to Sika Technical Dept. for direction.","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Applied product ready for use","t":"Temperature | Foot traffic | Light traffic | Full cure +10 °C | ~ 72 hours | ~ 6 days | ~ 10 days +20 °C | ~ 24 hours | ~ 4 days | ~ 7 days +30 °C | ~ 18 hours | ~ 2 days | ~ 5 days","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Consumption","t":"Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14 system ( ~ 0.5-0.7 mm) Coating System | Product | Consumption Primer (optional) | 1 × Sikafloor-161/-160 | ~ 0.25-0.35 kg/m² (4-6m²/litre) 1st Coat | 1× Sikafloor-264/-264T AU | ~ 0.25-0.35 kg/m² (4-6m²/litre) Top Coat | 1 x Sikafloor 264/-264T AU | ~ 0.20-0.30 kg/m² (5-7m²/litre)","g":"Application consumption"},{"l":"SUBSTRATE QUALITY","t":"Substrate strength to produce a bond pull value of >1.5Mpa.","g":"Application steps"},{"l":"SUBSTRATE PREPARATION","t":"Subsrate should be prepared to CSP2 - approx 0.5mm in profile. Any imperfections greater than this should be filled using Sikafloor 160 or 161 with fillers.","g":"Application steps"},{"l":"APPLICATION","t":"Application of finish coat Sikafloor 264T AU should be by roller or Squeegee and back roll process. Ensure an even application by using correct roller equipment and rolling techniques. Observe pot life of mixes applied at the site as well joining wet edges with the appropriate timing. Failure to do any of the above will produce uneven texture and or colour. Refer to Sika Technical Dept. for direction","g":"Application steps"},{"l":"CLEANING","t":"Please refer to the Method Statement Sikafloor‐ Cleaning Regime","g":"Application steps"}]},"dc":[{"id":"d-66abe3fae4","t":"Sikafloor MultiDur ET-14","ty":"system_data_sheet","tl":"System Data Sheet (SDS)","v":"31/03/2023","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/e/sikafloor_multiduret-14.pdf","ok":true,"f":"PDF"}],"r":{"status":"published","ds":{"url":"https://aus.sik